---
id: org.dxos.plugin.chessCom
name: ChessComPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Chess.com account integration for DXOS Composer. Links a Chess.com username,
syncs archived games into a local feed as `Game` objects (chess variant), and
displays them in a masonry gallery rendered by plugin-chess game cards.

## Extensions

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`       |

## Types

```mdl
type ChessComAccount
  fields:
    username: string @label/title
    playerId?: number
    profileUrl?: string
    followers?: number
    country?: string
    lastOnline?: number
    joined?: number
    status?: string
    isStreamer?: boolean
    verified?: boolean
    league?: string
    streamingPlatforms?: string[]
    games: Ref<Feed>   # Game (org.dxos.type.game) entries with Chess.State variants
  foreignKeys:
    service: chess.com
    id: <username>
  typename: org.dxos.type.chessCom.account
  version: 0.1.0
```

## Components

```mdl
component ChessGameArticle
  desc: Masonry gallery of synced chess games; each tile renders a Game card surface.
  props:
    account: ChessComAccount
  actions:
    syncGames()
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ [Sync games] toolbar    │
    ├─────────────────────────┤
    │ masonry of game cards   │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

## Operations

```mdl
op SyncGames
  key: org.dxos.operation.chessCom.syncGames
  desc: Fetch all archived games from chess.com and append new Game objects to the account feed.
  input:
    account: Ref<ChessComAccount>
  output:
    appended: number
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]

op ClearSyncedGames
  key: org.dxos.operation.chessCom.clearSyncedGames
  desc: Replace the account games feed with a fresh empty feed, discarding synced games.
  input:
    account: Ref<ChessComAccount>
  output:
    removed: number
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Create account

  req F-1.1: Create form asks only for Chess.com username.
  req F-1.2: Account is stamped with foreign key `{ source: chess.com, id: username }`.
  req F-1.3: A backing ECHO feed is created for synced games.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Sync games

  req F-2.1: SyncGames loads player profile fields from the chess.com Published API.
  req F-2.2: SyncGames walks monthly archives and imports each game as a `Game` with `Chess.State` (PGN/FEN).
  req F-2.3: Re-sync does not duplicate games already present in the feed (uuid foreign key).
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Game gallery

  req F-3.1: ChessGameArticle lists games from the account feed in a masonry layout.
  req F-3.2: Each tile renders `AppSurface.CardContent` so plugin-chess supplies the game card.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Create with username only
  given: user enters username "hhhhthrv"
  then:
    - ChessComAccount.username === "hhhhthrv"
    - foreign key chess.com/hhhhthrv is set
```

```mdl
test T-2: Sync deduplicates games
  given: account with two games already synced
  when: SyncGames runs against the same upstream archive
  then: appended === 0
```

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Link a Chess.com account and sync games
  desc: The core round-trip — create the account, sync its archived games, then clear them back out.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, T-1, T-2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-chess-com is enabled — it is OFF by default, and no chess.com operation is
      registered until it is on. Enabling is a UI action (Settings -> plugin registry);
      `manager.enable()` returns without error from the debug port and does not enable it.
    - a Chess.com username with at least one archived game (e.g. a well-known public account)
    - no ChessComAccount for that username exists in the space — ABORT rather than deleting one
      this flow did not create
    - account: the ChessComAccount object the human creates in step 1, resolved by the runner
      after that step so later steps can reference it — there is no create operation to `capture`
      it from
  test:
    - name: Create the account
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Chess.com Account. Enter the username.
      expect: a ChessComAccount with that username appears under the collection, its foreign key
        set to `{ source: chess.com, id: username }`
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — there is no create operation for the account, only `SyncGames` and
        `ClearSyncedGames` (see the Operations section); the account form is UI-only, matching
        plugin-chess's own game-creation gap. That is the finding, not an omission.
    - name: Sync games
      do: Click "Sync games" in the account's toolbar.
      invoke: [op:SyncGames] { account: Ref.make($given.account) }
      capture: synced
      expect: the masonry gallery fills with game cards, one per archived game, and the account's
        profile fields (followers, country, joined, ...) populate
      assert: return $result.appended > 0;
    - name: Re-sync does not duplicate
      do: Click "Sync games" again.
      invoke: [op:SyncGames] { account: Ref.make($given.account) }
      expect: the gallery is unchanged — no duplicate tiles appear
      assert: return $result.appended === 0;
  after:
    - name: Clear synced games
      do: Use the account's "Clear synced games" action.
      invoke: [op:ClearSyncedGames] { account: Ref.make($given.account) }
      expect: the gallery is empty
      assert: return $result.removed > 0;
    - name: Delete the account
      do: Right-click the account in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$given.account], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree
```
